# Limits and corrections

The two opt-in browser tests were not run because CIEL_TEST_BROWSER was not configured. This task changes no UI. Real loopback REST and SSE controllers, MCP dispatch, real temporary stores, historical reader imports and the real packaged side-intake.js/backend integration were exercised; no claude.exe or real upstream model was launched.

An initially launched redundant full eight-file before run was stopped after stale JS barriers reached their timeout. Its Python driver and its exact Node/Python descendants were identified and stopped; parent baseline and other processes were untouched. Existing unit evidence plus a bounded four-method in-memory HEAD-fixture replay provides the before evidence.

A preliminary claim that advice question output was a product redaction defect was withdrawn after reading the explicit public projection contract. The product redactor was not changed.
